From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 20:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] unregister the p2p wiphy it fails to keep

Every probe registers a p2p role wiphy that remove never destroys, so the
probe after a host reset finds both role slots taken and frees its new
wiphy while still registered. The first regulatory change after the module
is gone then crashes:

  Unable to handle kernel paging request at virtual address ffff80007ab55fec
  wiphy_update_regulatory+0xd0/0xa10 [cfg80211]

Unregister it before freeing it.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
--- a/wlan/os/linux/gl_p2p.c
+++ b/wlan/os/linux/gl_p2p.c
@@ -1202,11 +1202,13 @@ BOOLEAN glP2pCreateWirelessDevice(P_GLUE_INFO_T prGlueInfo)
 
 	if (i == KAL_P2P_NUM) {
 		DBGLOG(INIT, WARN, "fail to register wiphy to driver\n");
-		goto free_wiphy;
+		goto unregister_wiphy;
 	}
 
 	return TRUE;
 
+unregister_wiphy:
+	wiphy_unregister(prWiphy);
 free_wiphy:
 	wiphy_free(prWiphy);
 free_wdev:
